Trip Fuel Planner
========================================================
author: Aman Hayat
date: 25 October 2026
css: pitch.css

Know the approximate fuel cost before you leave.

========================================================
Why plan fuel?

A distance alone does not tell you the cost of a journey.

The same trip can use very different amounts of fuel in different cars.

Trip Fuel Planner turns three familiar choices into a simple estimate.

========================================================
One screen, three inputs

- Pick a car from the built-in `mtcars` data.
- Set the distance in kilometres and price in rupees per litre.
- See litres, estimated cost, and a comparison chart update immediately.

The app explains these steps on its own page.

========================================================
The calculation is reproducible

The source dataset reports miles per US gallon. We convert it to kilometres per litre, then estimate fuel for a 250 km trip at ₹100 per litre.

```{r, echo=TRUE}
mpg <- mtcars["Toyota Corolla", "mpg"]
km_per_litre <- mpg * 0.425143707
litres <- 250 / km_per_litre
round(c(km_per_litre = km_per_litre,
        litres = litres, cost_rupees = litres * 100), 2)
```

========================================================
Try a route of your own

The chart compares the ten lowest estimated fuel costs for the chosen journey.

This is a teaching estimate using older cars. Road conditions and driving style change real consumption.

Open the live app from the assignment submission and try your own journey.

The full `ui.R` and `server.R` source accompanies the app on GitHub.
